Polar-KEM functional evaluation implementation
==============================================

This tree contains the official-API reference and portable optimized
implementations of PolarKEM-128, PolarKEM-256, and PolarKEM-512.  It provides
a reproducible implementation profile for interface integration, correctness
validation, known-answer testing, and preliminary performance evaluation.

Directory layout
----------------

* Reference_Implementation/PolarKEM-{128,256,512}
* Optimized_Implementation/PolarKEM-{128,256,512}

Every instance is self-contained.  In particular, each instance carries the
unmodified official API_PKC KAT driver and auxiliary implementation alongside
the Polar-KEM sources.  Do not replace the official files with local variants.

Official-file integrity (SHA-256)
--------------------------------

The following hashes identify the API_PKC files used for this rectification:

    KAT_KEM.c  62E33B3557C1D7BDB1F16FEA4FFA050829A502C4EDD0104813A0192FADA4213D
    auxfunc.c   27446371ECCF14383E5A333DFED6333ED9A2232580D0A52C1C681BC2074A8368
    auxfunc.h   39986E91D9AF503EAFB568B0C18E50EB9AB5FCECA140DDD26924343A09284E74
    drng.c      0DF0AC78C828BD43BF05724398FA530767D753AA7801A1D1FA5D621321EC797E
    drng.h      D758AA7F5618BB781960FB7193B536897A09B1FDD7ACCA5AD8A45495D0E147A7

Building all six directories
----------------------------

On a POSIX system with a C99 compiler and GNU-compatible make:

    ./build_all.sh
    ./build_all.sh --run
    ./build_all.sh --sanitize
    ./build_all.sh --clean

On Windows with GCC available on PATH:

    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\build_all.ps1
    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\build_all.ps1 -RunKAT
    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\build_all.ps1 -Sanitize
    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\build_all.ps1 -Clean

The normal build uses C99 plus -Wall, -Wextra, -Wpedantic, and -Werror.  The
sanitizer mode additionally enables AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer
where supported by the selected GCC/Clang toolchain.

Sanitizer waiver: ASan and UBSan instrument the official KAT driver and every
project-owned translation unit.  The checksummed official auxfunc.c and drng.c
also remain instrumented, but are compiled with -fno-sanitize=shift because the
upstream SM3 rotate macro contains a shift-by-32 expression.  Modifying that
macro would violate the byte-for-byte official-file requirement; all other
enabled ASan/UBSan checks remain active and the final executable links both
runtimes.

KAT output
----------

Running an instance creates output/KAT_KEM_PolarKEM-*.txt beneath that
instance directory.  The official driver creates ten records from its fixed
seed sequence.  Reference and optimized output for a parameter set must be
byte-for-byte identical.

Evaluation scope and specification alignment / 评估范围与规范对应
--------------------------------------------------------------

Only Construction D level 0 is active; all higher-level coefficients are
fixed to zero.  The public transform is represented by a compact public seed
for an exact signed permutation.  This choice supports functional consistency
testing.  PolarKEM-128 and PolarKEM-256 use q = 12289; PolarKEM-512 uses
q = 18433.  None of the instances uses an NTT.  The frozen submission paper
and rectification report are the normative sources for the algorithm design,
parameter rationale, and security analysis.

本目录代码用于官方接口集成、正确性验证、已知答案测试和初步性能评估。
算法设计、参数依据与安全性分析以冻结的算法文本及整改说明为准。

Security statement boundary / 安全声明边界
----------------------------------------

This README records implementation, build, and interoperability details.  It
does not add to or replace the security claims and analyses in the frozen
submission paper.  Evaluation and use of this implementation should therefore
be considered together with the paper and the rectification report.

本 README 仅说明实现、构建与接口互操作细节，不增加或替代冻结算法文本中的
安全性声明与分析。对本实现的评估和使用应结合算法文本及整改说明进行。
